xnu 0403: the UI hook can be injected into kbd and Spotlight, the keyboard's processes

The software keyboard draws correctly-sized keys (42 pt on a 48 pt pitch, the
480 pt layout) but on its first presentation puts the ten-key row at x 37.3 pt
instead of 3, so `p`, delete and `search` are clipped by the right edge. A later
layout pass corrects it in place. The host is not the source: SpringBoard's
UIKeyboardWillChangeFrameNotification reports 0,765.7 480x301, the keyboard's
scene layer is 480x1066.7 at 0,0 and the safe area is 59,0,34,0; the offset fits
a 512 pt scene whose 480 pt plane keeps its 3 pt margin (expected).

Which process lays that plane out was the open question. SpringBoard registers
the whole keyboard family (UIKeyboardLayoutStar, UIKeyboardLayout,
TUIKeyplaneView, UIKBKeyplaneView) and instantiates none of them for the
presented keyboard; kbd carries the input managers (TIKeyboard*) and no layout
class at all, even after the keyboard is up; the keyboard's surfaces are created
by the Spotlight process (`MONDRIAN SURF: Spotlight ... 1440x729`), which hosts
the search UI and its keyboard. Bit 11 therefore gives the hook to both kbd and
Spotlight. The bit is off in the default command line; a boot that reads the
keyboard's own geometry adds `mondrian_ui_hook=3334` (6 | 0x100 | 0x400 | 0x800)
with EXTRA_ARGS, and the last key wins.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
index 3dc87f4..3e1fdf0 100755
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5679,6 +5679,18 @@ bad:
  */
 #define MONDRIAN_HOOK_APP               0x400
 
+/*
+ * kbd and Spotlight (0x800): the two processes involved in the software
+ * keyboard. On the first presentation its ten-key row is laid out about 33 pt
+ * right of a 480 pt screen and the last column is clipped; the host is not the
+ * source -- SpringBoard's frame notification is 480x301 at x 0, the scene
+ * layer is 480 wide and the safe area has no horizontal inset (measured
+ * 2026-11-21). SpringBoard registers the layout classes and instantiates none
+ * of them, kbd has no layout class at all, and the keyboard's surfaces are
+ * created by the Spotlight process, so the probe has to reach both.
+ */
+#define MONDRIAN_HOOK_KBD               0x800
+
 /*
  * Does this boot's copy of a dylib exist in /private/var/vm? glblob=1 writes
  * them there once the root turns writable, so before that, or with glblob=0,
@@ -6110,6 +6122,12 @@ mondrian_ui_hook_env(struct image_params *imgp, char *env, size_t size)
 	} else if (imgp->ip_ndp->ni_cnd.cn_namelen == sizeof("xpcproxy") - 1 &&
 	    strncmp(name, "xpcproxy", sizeof("xpcproxy") - 1) == 0) {
 		wanted = MONDRIAN_HOOK_XPCPROXY;
+	} else if (wanted == 0 &&
+	    (mondrian_name_is(name, (size_t)imgp->ip_ndp->ni_cnd.cn_namelen,
